5.5  Performance descriptors

Performance descriptors give a general indication of likely levels of attainment by representative students
performing at boundaries: Distinction at Level 2, Pass at Level 2 and Pass at Level 1.

Performance descriptor – Distinction at Level 2

Students will be able to:

•	 Recall, select and apply detailed knowledge and

thorough understanding of information regarding
contemporary issues in sport

•	 Demonstrate detailed knowledge and thorough

understanding of social factors that affect
performance and participation in sporting activities

•	 Present information clearly and accurately, using a

wide range of terminology

•	 Apply relevant knowledge, understanding and

skills in a range of situations to plan and carry out a
wide range of suitable activities and exercises that
demonstrate personal ability in sporting activities
completed safely, reviewing their activities and
plans

Performance descriptor – Pass at Level 2

