4.4  Unit R186: Sport and the media

Aims

Sport uses the media to promote itself and in turn
the media uses sport to sell its products. Opinions are
moulded, role models created or rejected, and sports
performers can be made into celebrities. However, the
increased exposure of sports and performers may not
always be a positive experience.

Rapid development in technology is enabling sport
to be viewed, replayed and discussed whenever and
wherever the spectator wishes. You will learn how this

can be a good thing in some cases but not so good
from other points of view

In this unit you will learn to explore both sides of
these media sources and apply real life examples to
demonstrate the nature of the relationship between
media and sport. You will develop your ability to
evaluate and interpret the different ways sport is
represented by the media.

R186: Sport and the media

Topic Area 1: The different sources of media that cover sport

