5.2  Synoptic assessment

Synoptic assessment is a built-in feature of this
qualification. It means that students need to use
an appropriate selection of their knowledge,
understanding and skills developed across the
qualification in an integrated way and apply them to a
key task or tasks.

This also helps students to build a holistic
understanding of the subject and the connections
between different elements of learning, so they can go
on to apply what they learn from this qualification to
new and different situations and contexts.

The externally assessed unit R184 allows students to
gain underpinning knowledge and understanding
relevant to Exercise, Physical Activity, Sport and Health
sector, and the Non Examined Assessment (NEA) units
