rements

There is no requirement for students to achieve any specific qualifications before
taking this qualification.
Students must complete three units:

•	 One mandatory externally assessed unit (exam) - see the Terminal assessment

below

•	 One mandatory centre-assessed unit (NEA)

Assessment method/
model

•	 One optional centre-assessed unit (NEA) from a choice of two.
Unit R184 is assessed by an exam and marked by us.

You will assess the NEA units and we will moderate them.

We provide set assignments which must be used to assess the NEA units. Each set
assignment for units R186 and R187 will be valid for 1 year. The set assignment
for R185 is generic and will not be replaced each year, see section 6.2 for more
information. The dates for which assignments are live will be shown on the front
cover. You must make sure you use the live assignment for students’ assessments and
submit in the period in which it is live.

You must make sure students have an entry for each series in which you intend to
submit or resubmit an NEA unit.
•

January

•

June

The exam must be taken in the final assessment series before qualification
certification.

If a student retakes their qualification, they will need to resit the exam in order
to meet the terminal rule again. The first qualification grade is used for school
performance tables even if they have improved their qualification grade.

Assessment series
each year

