+    "value": "Award up to 4 marks. Credit must include at least two distinct safety-related uses of technology AND a named example:\n- GPS/wearable vests monitor training load, heart rate and sprint speeds, reducing overtraining and injury risk in football and rugby\n- Instrumented mouthguards in rugby measure head impacts and can alert medical staff to a possible concussion\n- Prosthetic carbon-fibre limbs allow Paralympic athletes to compete with reduced injury risk and improved mobility (named: Paralympic sprint blades)\n- Video analysis / slow-motion review allows medical teams to study injury mechanisms and inform prevention programmes\n- Rule changes informed by data analysis (e.g. high-tackle restrictions in rugby, informed by concussion data from RFU medical teams)\nA named example is required. An answer with no named technology is capped at 2 marks.",
