+    "field": "practice_questions",
+    "path": "[3].marks",
+    "expect": "Award up to 4 marks. Credit two distinct concerns with development:\n- Cost overruns: Olympic budgets almost always exceed initial estimates — Paris 2024 grew from ~3.6bn to ~8.8bn euros. Taxpayers fund the gap.\n- Displacement and community disruption: building venues requires relocating residents, often from lower-income areas, who may receive inadequate compensation.\n- Political opposition: public may resist via protest or referendum, causing reputational and governance problems for the host government.\n- Bid cost with no guarantee: a bid campaign alone costs tens of millions; a losing city gets nothing back.\nA named example is required for the top marks. An answer without any named example is capped at 2 marks.",
